@BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress = http://localhost:5166

### 1. Valid budget -> expect 201 Created with Spent and Remaining filled in
# @name createBudget

POST {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Groceries",
  "limit": 400.00,
  "expenses": [
    { "amount": 52.75, "description": "Costco run", "date": "2026-10-20" },
    { "amount": 18.40, "description": "Farmers market" }
  ]
}

### 2. Over the limit -> expect 400 BudgetExceededException
POST {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Dining out",
  "limit": 50.00,
  "expenses": [
    { "amount": 30.00, "description": "Tacos" },
    { "amount": 25.00, "description": "Sushi" }
  ]
}

### 3. Negative amount -> expect 400 InvalidAmountException
POST {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "name": "Gas",
  "limit": 100.00,
  "expenses": [
    { "amount": -10.00, "description": "Refund?" }
  ]
}

### 4. Missing name -> expect 400 from [ApiController], before our code runs
POST {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "limit": 100.00
}

### 5. Get the budget from request 1 -> expect 200 with the same data
# uses the id from request 1's response, so send request 1 first
GET {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets/{{createBudget.response.body.$.id}}

### 6. Unknown id -> expect 404 Not Found
GET {{BudgetTracker.API_HostAddress}}/api/budgets/00000000-0000-0000-0000-000000000000